whatsup-desktop (1.2.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Add a light or dark Style setting (Settings, General, Appearance).
  * Explain a missing tray icon in Settings. Debian turns off the MATE
    panel's tray support for icons like WhatsUp's; the hint turns it back
    on, or shows how in a terminal or dconf Editor.

 -- Maarten van der Rijst <claude@feedmebits.nl>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:30:00 +0200

whatsup-desktop (1.1.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * First Debian stable (trixie) release. Built with --no-default-features so
    the keyboard shortcuts dialog uses the libadwaita 1.7 fallback, since
    Debian stable has no AdwShortcutsDialog (libadwaita 1.8).

 -- Maarten van der Rijst <claude@feedmebits.nl>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 19:30:00 +0200
